### Bug Summary

`api/helpers/game-states/get-log.js` incorrectly processes game states where a five resolves, outputting text including `NaN` instead of the number of cards drawn

### Detailed Description

![Image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/8528efb8-2d2f-47ed-abc1-5b56e089b680)

This function inside `get-log` is responsible for generating the text shown above

```
      const getResolveFiveMessage = () => {
        const previousRow = game.gameStates[i - 1] ?? null;
        const amountOfCardsDrawn =
        row[`p${row.playedBy}Hand`]?.length - previousRow[`p${row.playedBy}Hand`?.length];

        return amountOfCardsDrawn === 1 ? `draws 1 card` : `draws ${amountOfCardsDrawn} cards`;
      };
```

### Current Behavior

The game log for resolving a five includes `NaN` instead of the number of cards drawn

### Expected Behavior

It shows the correct number of cards drawn

### Steps to Reproduce

1. Play a 5 and resolve it
2. Look at the game log
